# The build context is sent to the daemon in full, so everything not needed for
# `go build` is latency at best — and a few of these would be a leak.

.git
.github

# ⚠ THE DANGEROUS ONES. A developer's working tree holds a real database with
# real tokens and a real credit ledger, and an uploaded-file directory beside it.
# Without these lines they are copied into the build context, and any layer that
# does `COPY . .` bakes them into an image.
*.db
*.db-shm
*.db-wal
blobs/
res/
data/

# Local scratch and scripts from a development session.
test/
*.sh
compose.yml
.env

# Documentation and records: read by people, never by the compiler.
docs/
README.md
*.md

# Built artefacts. A host binary is the wrong GOOS anyway.
bin/
routerbin
